            "heading": "Gulzar aur pottery workshop ke laal-kaale copper oxides",
            "headingHinglish": "Gulzar aur pottery workshop ke laal-kaale copper oxides",
            "body": "Gulzar apne Papa ke dost ke pottery glaze workshop mein gaya tha, jahan mitti ke bartan par chamakdar rang (glaze) chadhaya jaata hai. Shelf par do alag-alag band dibbon mein do powder rakhe the: ek **chamakdar laal (Cu₂O)** aur doosra **gehra kaala (CuO)**.\n\nGulzar ne label padha aur chaunk gaya: \"Uncle, dono dibbon par likha hai ki ye sirf **copper aur oxygen** se bane hain! Par Class 9 mein humne padha tha ki ek compound mein tatvon ka ratio fixed hota hai. To copper aur oxygen milkar do bilkul alag rang ke compounds kaise bana sakte hain?\"\n\nWorkshop wale uncle muskuraye: \"Shabaash Gulzar, yahi sawaal 1803 mein John Dalton ke dimaag mein aaya tha! Jab wahi do tatva ek se zyada compounds banayein — jaise laal copper(I) oxide (Cu₂O) aur kaala copper(II) oxide (CuO) — to unke andar oxygen ke mass mein koi ajeeb-o-gareeb number nahi hota, balki ek **simple whole-number ratio (1 : 2)** nikalta hai! Isi ko **Law of Multiple Proportions** kehte hain.\" Chalo, paanchon niyamon aur Dalton ke siddhant ko khol kar dekhte hain.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Gulzar apne Papa ke dost ke pottery glaze workshop mein gaya tha, jahan mitti ke bartan par chamakdar rang (glaze) chadhaya jaata hai. Shelf par do alag-alag band dibbon mein do powder rakhe the: ek **chamakdar laal (Cu₂O)** aur doosra **gehra kaala (CuO)**.\n\nGulzar ne label padha aur chaunk gaya: \"Uncle, dono dibbon par likha hai ki ye sirf **copper aur oxygen** se bane hain! Par Class 9 mein humne padha tha ki ek compound mein tatvon ka ratio fixed hota hai. To copper aur oxygen milkar do bilkul alag rang ke compounds kaise bana sakte hain?\"\n\nWorkshop wale uncle muskuraye: \"Shabaash Gulzar, yahi sawaal 1803 mein John Dalton ke dimaag mein aaya tha! Jab wahi do tatva ek se zyada compounds banayein — jaise laal copper(I) oxide (Cu₂O) aur kaala copper(II) oxide (CuO) — to unke andar oxygen ke mass mein koi ajeeb-o-gareeb number nahi hota, balki ek **simple whole-number ratio (1 : 2)** nikalta hai! Isi ko **Law of Multiple Proportions** kehte hain.\" Chalo, paanchon niyamon aur Dalton ke siddhant ko khol kar dekhte hain."
