            "heading": "Key Vocabulary & Terms",
            "headingHinglish": "Naye shabd",
            "body": "| Shabd | Matlab (simple bhasha mein) | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Charge-to-mass ratio (e/m)** | Kisi particle ke electric charge aur mass ka anupaat (unit: C/kg) | Electron ke liye 1.7588 × 10¹¹ C/kg (har gas mein same!) |\n| **Quantisation of charge** | Kisi bhi vastu par kul charge hamesha ek electron ke charge (e) ka poora-ank gunaj (q = n × e) hota hai | 3e ya 5e ho sakta hai, 1.5e kabhi nahi |\n| **Canal rays (Anode rays)** | Discharge tube mein bhari gas ke atoms se electrons nikalne ke baad bane positive ions ki dhaar | H₂ gas mein sabse halka positive ion = proton (H⁺) |\n| **Isotones** | Alag-alag tatvon ke aise atoms jinke nucleus mein **neutrons ki sankhya (A − Z) barabar** ho | ¹⁴C, ¹⁵N aur ¹⁶O (teeno mein 8 neutrons) |\n| **Isoelectronic species** | Aise alag atoms ya ions jinmein **kul electrons ki ginti barabar** ho | N³⁻, O²⁻, F⁻, Na⁺, Mg²⁺ (sabmein 10 electrons) |",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Shabd | Matlab (simple bhasha mein) | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Charge-to-mass ratio (e/m)** | Kisi particle ke electric charge aur mass ka anupaat (unit: C/kg) | Electron ke liye 1.7588 × 10¹¹ C/kg (har gas mein same!) |\n| **Quantisation of charge** | Kisi bhi vastu par kul charge hamesha ek electron ke charge (e) ka poora-ank gunaj (q = n × e) hota hai | 3e ya 5e ho sakta hai, 1.5e kabhi nahi |\n| **Canal rays (Anode rays)** | Discharge tube mein bhari gas ke atoms se electrons nikalne ke baad bane positive ions ki dhaar | H₂ gas mein sabse halka positive ion = proton (H⁺) |\n| **Isotones** | Alag-alag tatvon ke aise atoms jinke nucleus mein **neutrons ki sankhya (A − Z) barabar** ho | ¹⁴C, ¹⁵N aur ¹⁶O (teeno mein 8 neutrons) |\n| **Isoelectronic species** | Aise alag atoms ya ions jinmein **kul electrons ki ginti barabar** ho | N³⁻, O²⁻, F⁻, Na⁺, Mg²⁺ (sabmein 10 electrons) |"
