            "heading": "Common Exam Mistakes (Watch Out!)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "1. **Galti 1: Ye soch lena ki canal rays (anode rays) ka e/m bhi cathode rays ki tarah har gas ke liye constant hota hai.**\n   Cathode rays sirf electrons se bani hain, isliye unka e/m (1.7588 × 10¹¹ C/kg) har gas mein same hai. Par **canal rays** gas ke bache hue positive ions (H⁺, He⁺, Ne⁺) se banti hain jinka mass alag-alag hota hai — isliye canal rays ka e/m gas badalne par badal jaata hai!\n\n2. **Galti 2: Isotopes, Isobars aur Isotones ke aksharon mein gadbadi.**\n   Aasaan yaad karne ki trick: Iso**p**es → same **p**rotons (Z); Iso**b**ars → same **b**haar / mass number (A); Iso**n**es → same **n**eutrons (A − Z).\n\n3. **Galti 3: Positive ion (cation) mein electrons jodne ki galti.**\n   Mg²⁺ (Z = 12) mein ek student ne \"+2 dekh kar 12 + 2 = 14 electrons\" likh diya!\n   *Sahi baat:* Positive charge (+) tab aata hai jab negative electrons **bahar nikal jaayein**. Isliye Mg²⁺ mein 12 − 2 = **10 electrons** hain!",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. **Galti 1: Ye soch lena ki canal rays (anode rays) ka e/m bhi cathode rays ki tarah har gas ke liye constant hota hai.**\n   Cathode rays sirf electrons se bani hain, isliye unka e/m (1.7588 × 10¹¹ C/kg) har gas mein same hai. Par **canal rays** gas ke bache hue positive ions (H⁺, He⁺, Ne⁺) se banti hain jinka mass alag-alag hota hai — isliye canal rays ka e/m gas badalne par badal jaata hai!\n\n2. **Galti 2: Isotopes, Isobars aur Isotones ke aksharon mein gadbadi.**\n   Aasaan yaad karne ki trick: Iso**p**es → same **p**rotons (Z); Iso**b**ars → same **b**haar / mass number (A); Iso**n**es → same **n**eutrons (A − Z).\n\n3. **Galti 3: Positive ion (cation) mein electrons jodne ki galti.**\n   Mg²⁺ (Z = 12) mein ek student ne \"+2 dekh kar 12 + 2 = 14 electrons\" likh diya!\n   *Sahi baat:* Positive charge (+) tab aata hai jab negative electrons **bahar nikal jaayein**. Isliye Mg²⁺ mein 12 − 2 = **10 electrons** hain!"
