            "headingHinglish": "Naye shabd",
            "body": "| Shabd | Matlab (simple bhasha mein) | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Aufbau principle** | Ground state mein electrons hamesha sabse kam energy wale orbital se badhti energy ke kram mein bharte hain | 1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p → 4s → 3d |\n| **(n + l) rule (Bohr-Bury)** | Multi-electron atom mein jiska (n + l) chhota, uski energy kam; (n + l) barabar ho to chhote n wale ki energy kam | 4s (4+0 = 4) < 3d (3+2 = 5) |\n| **Pauli Exclusion Principle** | Ek hi atom ke koi bhi do electrons ke chaaron quantum numbers (n, l, mₗ, mₛ) ek jaise nahi ho sakte | Ek orbital mein max 2 electrons: ek ↑ (+½) aur ek ↓ (−½) |\n| **Hund's Rule of Maximum Multiplicity** | Barabar energy (degenerate) orbitals mein pairing tab tak nahi hoti jab tak har orbital mein 1-1 electron parallel spin ke saath na bhar jaaye | Nitrogen 2p³: [↑][↑][↑] (3 unpaired) |\n| **Exchange energy** | Ek hi subshell mein parallel spin wale electrons ke aapas mein jagah badalne (exchange) se milne wali extra stability | 3d⁵ mein 10 exchange pairs (3d⁴ ke 6 pairs se zyada!) |",
