            "headingHinglish": "Naye shabd",
            "body": "| Shabd | Matlab (simple bhasha mein) | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Moseley's law** | Tatvon se nikalne wali X-rays ki frequency ke square root (√ν) ka atomic number Z ke saath seedhi rekha (straight line) ka rishta | √ν = a(Z − b) |\n| **Modern Periodic Law** | Tatvon ke physical aur chemical gun unke **atomic numbers (Z)** ke periodic functions hote hain | Moseley (1913) dwara siddh |\n| **IUPAC systematic name** | Z > 100 wale naye tatvon ko permanent naam milne se pehle unke digits ke Latin/Greek roots se diya gaya temporary naam | Z = 104 → Unnilquadium (Unq) |\n| **Digit roots** | 0 se 9 tak ke digits ke liye IUPAC ke fix shabd (nil, un, bi, tri, quad, pent, hex, sept, oct, enn) | 1 = un, 2 = bi, 9 = enn |\n| **Superheavy elements** | Z > 100 wale manav-nirmit, bahut unstable aur radioactive tatva (sirf padhne ke liye; lab mein nahi milte) | Z = 104 se Z = 118 tak |",
