            "bodyHinglish": "Ab tak humne aise salts dekhe jo paani mein aasani se ghul jaate hain (NaCl, KNO₃). Par kuch salts — jaise **AgCl, BaSO₄, PbCl₂, CaF₂, Mg(OH)₂** — paani mein behad kam ghulte hain (**sparingly soluble**, solubility < 0.01 M)! Inka ek chhota sa hissa ghulkar ions banata hai aur bacha hua solid tal mein baithkar ek **heterogeneous ionic equilibrium** bana leta hai — jise **Solubility Product (K_sp)** se naapa jaata hai! Aaj hum K_sp aur molar solubility **S** ka pakka rishta, **Q_sp vs K_sp** se precipitation check, common ion ka solubility par asar aur salt-analysis mein selective precipitation seekhenge."
