            "headingHinglish": "Naye shabd",
            "body": "| Shabd | Matlab (simple bhasha mein) | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Inductive effect (I)** | Electronegativity ke antar se **σ-electrons** ka permanent khisakna (3–4 carbons ke baad lagbhag khatam!) | −I (kheenchne wale): −NO₂, −CN, −F, −Cl; +I (dene wale): −C(CH₃)₃ > −CH(CH₃)₂ > −C₂H₅ > −CH₃ |\n| **Resonance / Mesomeric effect (R / M)** | Conjugated **π-electrons** ya lone pair ka permanent delocalisation (doori se kamzor NAHI hota!) | +R: −OH, −NH₂, −OCH₃; −R: −NO₂, −CHO, −COOH, −CN |\n| **Electromeric effect (E)** | Attacking reagent ki maang par π-bond ke electrons ka **poora, temporary transfer** (+E: reagent ki taraf; −E: reagent se door!) | H⁺ aane par C=C ke π-electrons ek C par shift hona |\n| **Hyperconjugation (H)** | **No-bond resonance:** Adjacent sp³ C−H ke **σ-electrons** ka khaali p-orbital (carbocation) ya π* orbital (alkene) ke saath overlap! | Jitne zyada **α-Hydrogens**, utni zyada stability! |",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Shabd | Matlab (simple bhasha mein) | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Inductive effect (I)** | Electronegativity ke antar se **σ-electrons** ka permanent khisakna (3–4 carbons ke baad lagbhag khatam!) | −I (kheenchne wale): −NO₂, −CN, −F, −Cl; +I (dene wale): −C(CH₃)₃ > −CH(CH₃)₂ > −C₂H₅ > −CH₃ |\n| **Resonance / Mesomeric effect (R / M)** | Conjugated **π-electrons** ya lone pair ka permanent delocalisation (doori se kamzor NAHI hota!) | +R: −OH, −NH₂, −OCH₃; −R: −NO₂, −CHO, −COOH, −CN |\n| **Electromeric effect (E)** | Attacking reagent ki maang par π-bond ke electrons ka **poora, temporary transfer** (+E: reagent ki taraf; −E: reagent se door!) | H⁺ aane par C=C ke π-electrons ek C par shift hona |\n| **Hyperconjugation (H)** | **No-bond resonance:** Adjacent sp³ C−H ke **σ-electrons** ka khaali p-orbital (carbocation) ya π* orbital (alkene) ke saath overlap! | Jitne zyada **α-Hydrogens**, utni zyada stability! |"
