            "heading": "Part A: Alkenes ki 4 Preparation Methods + Saytzeff's Rule",
            "headingHinglish": "Part A: Alkenes ki 4 Preparation Methods + Saytzeff's Rule",
            "body": "1. **Alkynes ka Partial Reduction (Stereoselective!):**\n   - **Lindlar's catalyst (Pd/C + quinoline):** Alkyne + H₂ → ***cis*-Alkene**!\n   - **Birch-type reduction (Na / liquid NH₃):** Alkyne + 2[H] → ***trans*-Alkene**!\n2. **Dehydrohalogenation of Alkyl Halides (β-Elimination with alc. KOH):**\n   - R−CH₂−CH₂−X + alc. KOH —(Δ)→ R−CH=CH₂ + KX + H₂O.\n   - **Saytzeff's Rule:** Jab 2 alag alkenes ban sakte hon, to **zyada substituted (zyada α-H wala)** alkene **major** hota hai!\n3. **Dehalogenation of Vicinal Dihalides:** CH₂Br−CH₂Br + **Zn** → CH₂=CH₂ + ZnBr₂.\n4. **Acidic Dehydration of Alcohols:** CH₃−CH₂−OH —(conc. H₂SO₄, 443 K)→ CH₂=CH₂ + H₂O *(also obeys Saytzeff's rule!)*.",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. **Alkynes ka Partial Reduction (Stereoselective!):**\n   - **Lindlar's catalyst (Pd/C + quinoline):** Alkyne + H₂ → ***cis*-Alkene**!\n   - **Birch-type reduction (Na / liquid NH₃):** Alkyne + 2[H] → ***trans*-Alkene**!\n2. **Dehydrohalogenation of Alkyl Halides (β-Elimination with alc. KOH):**\n   - R−CH₂−CH₂−X + alc. KOH —(Δ)→ R−CH=CH₂ + KX + H₂O.\n   - **Saytzeff's Rule:** Jab 2 alag alkenes ban sakte hon, to **zyada substituted (zyada α-H wala)** alkene **major** hota hai!\n3. **Dehalogenation of Vicinal Dihalides:** CH₂Br−CH₂Br + **Zn** → CH₂=CH₂ + ZnBr₂.\n4. **Acidic Dehydration of Alcohols:** CH₃−CH₂−OH —(conc. H₂SO₄, 443 K)→ CH₂=CH₂ + H₂O *(also obeys Saytzeff's rule!)*."
